lapse to one mean per collar in a 12-row collar-level table with sessions=3 each, and runs the exact Mann-Whitney U test on the 12 collar means (n = 6 vs 6), not on the 36 session rows.\",\"Reported numbers were verified against the data: collar means and group means (14.00 vs 9.10) are correct; U = 35 matches the single overlapping pair (DRN-04 mean 12.30 > INT-05 mean 11.80), exact two-sided p = 4/924 = 0.004329, and CLES = 35/36 = 0.972.\",\"The minted lock authorizes key columns [\\\"collar_id\\\"], exactly matching the declared independent-unit column for the same input digest, analysis, and mannwhitneyu procedure, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["Declared independent-unit column collar_id is consistent with the frozen data: each of 12 collars appears exactly three times (sessions 1-3) and treatment is fixed within collar, with identical 3-per-collar nesting in both the intact and drained arms (6 collars each).","The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue: it states sessions are repeated measurements of the same collar, shows the collapse to one mean per collar in a 12-row collar-level table with sessions=3 each, and runs the exact Mann-Whitney U test on the 12 collar means (n = 6 vs 6), not on the 36 session rows.","Reported numbers were verified against the data: collar means and group means (14.00 vs 9.10) are correct; U = 35 matches the single overlapping pair (DRN-04 mean 12.30 > INT-05 mean 11.80), exact two-sided p = 4/924 = 0.004329, and CLES = 35/36 = 0.972.","The minted lock authorizes key columns [\"collar_id\"], exactly matching the declared independent-unit column for the same input digest, analysis, and mannwhitneyu procedure, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone."]},"ttft_ms":11033,"ttft_stream_ms":1650,"time_to_request_ms":18,"type":"r